/**
@defgroup libopenwch libopenwch
@brief Project-wide documentation root.

libopenwch groups its public API by device family and by core or peripheral
component.  Start at @ref peripheral_apis for the drivers.

@if ch5xx58x
Bluetooth LE applications should start at @ref BLE.
@endif
*/

/**
@defgroup peripheral_apis Peripheral APIs
@ingroup libopenwch
@brief Core and peripheral drivers.

This group contains the QingKe core layer and the device families.  A family
page lists register definitions, configuration constants, and driver
functions.  The same driver source is shared by all parts in a family; the
device database in <code>ld/devices.data</code> adds the part-specific memory
map and ISA flags at link time.
*/

/**
@defgroup qingke_file QingKe core
@ingroup peripheral_apis
@brief Architecture core support shared by every WCH family.

The QingKe layer corresponds to libopencm3's <code>cm3/</code> directory.  It
provides the reset path and vector table, the PFIC (WCH's NVIC-compatible
interrupt controller), SysTick, DWT, CSR access, synchronisation helpers, and
the assertion hook.
*/

/**
@defgroup qingke_nvic_isrprototypes Interrupt service routine prototypes
@ingroup qingke_file
@brief Weak ISR entry points generated from each family's <code>irq.json</code>.

The names are lower-case versions of the interrupt source names in the WCH
reference manual.  An application overrides the handler it needs; the weak
default implementation in the family's vector table does nothing.
*/

@if ch32v0
/**
@defgroup CH32V0 CH32V00x
@ingroup peripheral_apis
@brief Drivers for the CH32V002/003/004/005/006/007 family.

These parts use the QingKe V2 core in RV32EC mode with 16 registers and
compressed instructions.  Ports are eight bits wide and each pin is configured
by one opaque four-bit nibble in the GPIO configuration register; see
@ref gpio_defines and @ref gpio_file.

The family archive is <code>libopenwch_ch32v0.a</code>.
*/

/**
@defgroup CH32V0_defines CH32V00x definitions
@ingroup CH32V0
@brief Register bit definitions, constants, and types for the CH32V00x family.
*/
@endif

@if ch5xx58x
/**
@defgroup CH5XX58X CH58x
@ingroup peripheral_apis
@brief Drivers for the CH582/583/584/585 family.

These parts use the QingKe V4 core in RV32IMAC mode.  A 32 MHz HSE crystal is
mandatory, most control registers are RWA (write-protected), and code that
reconfigures flash or enters low-power states must run from RAM through
<code>OPENWCH_HIGH_CODE</code>.

The family archive is <code>libopenwch_ch5xx58x.a</code>.  The optional BLE
wrapper links separately against WCH's Apache-2.0 binary; see @ref BLE.
*/

/**
@defgroup CH5XX58X_defines CH58x definitions
@ingroup CH5XX58X
@brief Register bit definitions, constants, and types for the CH58x family.
*/

/**
@defgroup BLE Bluetooth LE
@ingroup libopenwch
@brief Thin wrapper around WCH's closed-source BLE stack.

The wrapper documents and renames the subset of WCH's <code>LIBCH58xBLE.a</code>
API that a peripheral role needs.  It keeps WCH's event-driven TMOS model and
does not reimplement Bluetooth.  Applications must link the vendor archive and
the mini libc; the application template does that with
<code>LIBOPENWCH_BLE=1</code>.  The binary remains under WCH's Apache-2.0
licence.
*/
@endif
